<section class="hero">
  <h1>choudoufu <img class="hero-icon" src="choudoufu-inline-64.png" alt="" width="64" height="64"></h1>
  <p class="tagline">IAM-governed state for OpenTofu.</p>
</section>

<div class="landing-card">

<section class="lead">
  <p class="versions">Experimental, AWS only. Built on <strong>OpenTofu {{.UpstreamVersion}}</strong>
  (fork point
  <a href="https://github.com/opentofu/opentofu/commit/03743ce6e8"><code>03743ce6e8</code></a>).</p>

  <!-- The canonical description paragraph (#113): identical wording in
       README.md's opening, this lead, and the GitHub repo description.
       Change all three together or none. -->
  <p>Each resource carries its own ownership record as ordinary cloud tags.
  AWS can tell you what an estate contains. Your IAM already decides who may
  read or change it.</p>

  <p class="claim">An estate is inherited by being granted access to it.</p>

  <p>Handover is granting a role. Splitting an estate in two is rewriting
  tags. Whoever inherits one can list what they got with any cloud tool
  before running anything.</p>
</section>

<section class="demo">
  <h2>Prove it in two minutes</h2>
  <p>Paste this to a coding agent. It stands up a real estate against a local
  AWS emulator and checks each claim above. The exit code is the verdict.</p>
  <pre><code>Clone https://github.com/INTENTIUS/choudoufu, then do the following.

1. Confirm Docker is running (`docker info` must succeed).
2. If Go is installed, skip this step. Otherwise download the latest
   release tarball for this platform from
   https://github.com/INTENTIUS/choudoufu/releases, extract it, and
   export TOFU_BIN=&lt;absolute path to the extracted choudoufu binary&gt;.
3. From the repo root, run: bash live/e2e/run.sh --expect 5
4. Report each step's result as the script prints it, and the final exit code.

Exit code 0 means every claim the script makes about live resource markers
held. Non-zero means one of them did not. Report which step failed.</code></pre>
  <p class="next"><a href="compatibility.html">Will my config work?</a>
  &middot; <a href="migrate.html">Migrate an existing estate</a>
  &middot; <a href="start.html">Start a new one</a></p>
</section>

